    <Notes ShowOnLoad="0" Notes="TCE1:TCE-SC-20261014-A1&#10;Hardware: JPT YDFLP-E-60-M7-M-R 60 W, serial MC2BDJD71684; lens: F-Theta 174 mm; material: titanium (link the exact grade and batch in the experiment record).&#10;Hardware/process-envelope test, not a titanium colour chart. JPT YDFLP-E-60-M7-M-R with F-Theta 174 mm. Seven power groups P5/10/20/30/50/75/100%; within every group the eight horizontal strokes run top-to-bottom at V500/1000/1500/2000/3000/5000/7500/10000 mm/s. Each Line is 53 mm long so higher commanded speeds have enough run-up distance. Fixed F48 kHz, Q-Pulse 200 ns and one pass. Compare the onset of a repeatable track and the highest speed that still produces a continuous mark. Values above the controller/galvo limit may be clamped or rejected. A photo does not measure optical watts; use a calibrated power meter for output power. The titanium track is a surface-response observation, not colour matching.&#10;Canvas 76 x 56 mm; registered bounds 98 x 93.5 mm. First: full-area cross-hatched cleaning, 20% / 48 kHz / 2000 mm/s / 200 ns / 0.05 mm; second: black marker/label layer 25% / 60 kHz / 150 mm/s / 200 ns / 0.01 mm, one pass."/>
